# The published demo. Regenerate docs/index.html with:
#   uv run python -m scribe.build_demo
#
# Every `say` comes BEFORE the ops it describes: a line keeps playing over
# whatever is drawn next, so this is what makes the board move while the voice
# runs. Lines stacked after their own shapes are captions, and the board sits
# still for them.
board 64 36

say "A question with a more interesting answer than it looks."
text 3,2.5 "Why is the first visit always the slow one?"

say "Your browser asks a server, the server asks a database. Nothing exotic."
icon user 9,13 6 "you"
icon server 31,13 6 "origin"
icon db 53,13 6 "database"

say "Watch the numbers. The hop across the ocean costs forty times the hop across the room."
connect "you" "origin" "~80ms"
connect "origin" "database" "~2ms"

say "And that whole round trip only bought you the HTML."
text 3,22 "One trip per file -- and each one waits its turn."
box 8,25 11,2.4 "HTML"
say "Each file has to arrive before the browser knows to ask for the next one."
box 21,28 11,2.4 "then CSS"
box 34,31 11,2.4 "then JS"
highlight "then JS" "By here you have paid for the crossing four times over."

pan 36
say "Almost everyone reaches for this one."
text 3,39 "So the obvious fix:"
box 7,43 24,3.2 "buy faster internet"
strike "buy faster internet" "It does not help, and it is worth knowing why."
say "A wider pipe moves more at once. It does not shorten the ocean."
text 3,49 "Bandwidth is how WIDE the pipe is. This is how LONG it is."

say "So you do not speed up the journey. You move the destination closer."
icon globe 12,57 6 "edge"
icon user 40,57 6 "visitor"
connect "visitor" "edge" "~8ms"
say "That is a CDN, and that is the whole idea."
note 3,64 30 "Second visit is fast because nothing travels. The files are already down the road."
